<<<
vend makes vendible; see -ABLE 2. Vendor & vender are both in frequent use, with a tendency to DIFFEREN- TIATION; -or is better when the contrast or relation between seller & buyer is prominent, & -er when purveyor or dealer is all that is meant.
===
**vend** makes *vendible*; see ^^-ABLE^^ 2. *Vendor* & *vender* are both in frequent use, with a tendency to ^^DIFFERENTIATION^^; *-or* is better when the contrast or relation between seller & buyer is prominent, & *-er* when purveyor or dealer is all that is meant.
>>>

